unted structural vibration sensors, into a translunar trajectory. However, the Moon would not be in position for a translunar flight, and the Service Module engine would be fired about five minutes later to slow the craft, dropping its apogee to 11,989 nautical miles (22,204 km) and causing the CSM to return to Earth, simulating a \"direct-return\" abort. On the return leg, the engine would fire once more to accelerate the craft to simulate the nominal lunar return trajectory with a re-entry angle of -6.5 degrees and velocity of 36,500 feet per second (11,100 m/s). The entire mission would last about 10 hours.","orbit":"Elliptical Orbit","image":"https://thespacedevs-prod.nyc3.digitaloceanspaces.com/media/images/saturn2520v_image_20190222030036.jpeg","lsp":"National Aeronautics and Space Administration","pad":"Launch Complex 39A","location":"Kennedy Space Center, FL, USA","lat":"28.60822681","lon":"-80.60428186","pad_wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kennedy_Space_Center_Launch_Complex_39#Launch_Pad_39A","pad_map":"https://www.google.com/maps?q=28.60822681,-80.60428186","net_precision":"","webcast":false,"webcast_url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1Tv9HiuWc5A","hold_reason":"","fail_reason":"","weather":"","type":"detailed","program":["Apollo"],"orbital_count":815,"year_orbital":27,"window_start":"1968-04-04T12:00:01Z","window_end":"1968-04-04T12:00:01Z","probability":null,"boosters":[]},{"id":"ee7973c5-3461-4a23-bed1-53128971d6ee","name":"Atlas F | OV1-13 & 14","net":"1968-04-06T09:59:42Z","status":"Launch Successful","rocket":"SM-65F Atlas","mission":"OV1-13 & 14","mission_desc":"The OV1 (Orbiting Vehicle 1) were small research satellite to be launched piggy back on Atlas ICBM test flights. They consisted in general of the OV1 satellite and the OV1-PM propulsion module (or upper stage) to reach orbit.","orbit":"Low Earth Orbit","image":null,"lsp":"United States Air Force","pad":"576A2","location":"Vandenberg SFB, CA, USA","lat":"34.7394444","lon":"-120.62136